title: 'pallet-revive: bound storage deposit refunds by the held deposit'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    A refund for removed contract storage is now bounded by the storage deposit the contract
    holds above its base deposit. The refund is still computed pro rata from the item and byte
    deposits recorded in the contract's `ContractInfo`, but at the end of the call stack at most
    the contract's `StorageDepositReserve` hold minus its `storage_base_deposit` is paid out. The
    base deposit stays on hold until the contract is terminated. The bound uses
    `Deposit::total_on_hold`, which for `PGasDeposit` is the sum of the native and PGAS holds.

    The storage deposit reported by `bare_call`, `bare_instantiate`, dry runs and Ethereum
    receipts is now the amount released from the contracts' holds. When a refund is not
    released in full, the deposit limit is checked again against what is actually paid before
    any charge is paid, and the call fails with `StorageDepositNotEnoughFunds` if it is
    exceeded.

    With the native deposit backend (`()`), nothing changes for contracts whose recorded item
    and byte deposits match their hold. With `PGasDeposit`, an origin that is not entitled to
    the native part of a refund can see a smaller reported refund, and its deposit limit is
    enforced against what is actually paid. Previously the full requested refund was reported
    and counted against the limit although only part of it was released.

    No migration, configuration or runtime integration change is needed.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    The refund for removed contract storage never exceeds the deposit the contract holds above
    its base deposit, and the storage deposit reported for a call is the amount that was
    released from the contracts' holds. On runtimes using the native deposit backend, nothing
    changes for contracts whose deposit records match their hold. On runtimes using
    `PGasDeposit`, an origin that is not entitled to the native part of a refund can see a
    smaller reported refund, and its storage deposit limit is enforced against what is actually
    paid. A call whose limit is exceeded this way fails with `StorageDepositNotEnoughFunds`.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: minor
